          "id": "q",
          "label": "Evaporation Heat (q)",
          "unit": "kJ",
          "formula": "inputs.he * inputs.m",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "conversion_info",
      "content": "## Unit Conversion\n\n1 kJ/kg = 0.43 Btu/lbm = 0.24 kcal/kg\n\n## Formula\n\nThe heat required to evaporate a fluid:\n\n**q = he × m**\n\nWhere:\n- **q** = evaporation heat (kJ)\n- **he** = latent heat of evaporation (kJ/kg)\n- **m** = mass of liquid (kg)\n\n## Example\n\nFor 10 kg of water with latent heat of evaporation of 2256 kJ/kg:\n\nq = 2256 kJ/kg × 10 kg = **22,560 kJ**"
    }
